Workaround:
-------------------------------------------------------------------
The correct description of the variables is as follows:

CONST(NmOsek_NodeConfigType, NMOSEK_APPL_CONST)  NmOsek_ConfigMaskTable[][sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfig) / sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfigType)];
CONST(NmOsek_NodeConfigType, NMOSEK_APPL_CONST)  NmOsek_TargetConfigTable[][sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfig) / sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfigType)];


In which:

*The first dimension corresponds to:
The index of the table of the corresponding array


*The second dimension corresponds to:
The configuration byte



/**********************************************************************************************************************
 *  Example of the ROM tables provided by the application:
 *********************************************************************************************************************/
CONST(NmOsek_NodeConfigType, NMOSEK_APPL_CONST) NmOsek_ConfigMaskTable[2][sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfig) / sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfigType)] = 
{
  {
    0x69u,
    0x00u,
    0x80u,
    0x80u
  },
  {

    0x02u,
    0x12u,
    0x11u,
    0x40u
   }
};

CONST(NmOsek_NodeConfigType, NMOSEK_APPL_CONST) NmOsek_TargetConfigTable[2][sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfig) / sizeof(NmOsek_NodeConfigType)] = 
{
  {
    0xF9u,
    0x00u,
    0x80u,
    0x80u

  },
  {

    0x0Fu,
    0x12u,
    0x11u,
    0xC1u
   }
};

Workaround: ------------------------------------------------------------------- Create a User Config File for the Nm module with the following content: extern Std_ReturnType NmOsek_SetSleepReadyBit( CONST( NetworkHandleType, AUTOMATIC ) nmChannelHandle, CONST( boolean, AUTOMATIC ) nmSleepReadyBit );
Configure this User Config File in the 'User Config File' (/MICROSAR/Nm/NmGlobalConfig/NmGlobalProperties/NmUserConfigFile) setting in the NmGlobalProperties container in the 'Basic Editor' / 'Network Management General' editor in DaVinci Configurator.
Then create a stub implementation in a C File of this function: Std_ReturnType NmOsek_SetSleepReadyBit( CONST( NetworkHandleType, AUTOMATIC ) nmChannelHandle, CONST( boolean, AUTOMATIC ) nmSleepReadyBit ) { return E_OK; }
Resolution: ------------------------------------------------------------------- The described issue is corrected by modification of all affected work-products.

Workaround:
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Use a user-configuration file to override and adapt the API to match the expected prototype.

1) Create a user-configuration file (e.g. dcm.cfg). Refer to the DCM technical reference on how to use such a file.
2) Add the following content to it:

/* WA_ESCAN00100457_BEGIN: */
#if defined (DCM_SOURCE)
extern Std_ReturnType Dem_DcmGetDTCOfOBDFreezeFrame_Wrapper(uint8 FrameNumber, uint32* DTC);
# define Dem_DcmGetDTCOfOBDFreezeFrame Dem_DcmGetDTCOfOBDFreezeFrame_Wrapper
#endif
/* WA_ESCAN00100457_END: */

3) In an application C-source file (e.g. Appl<SourceFile>.c) add following code:

#include "Dcm.h"

/* WA_ESCAN00100457_BEGIN: */
/**
 *  (AR <= 4.2.1) to (AR >= 4.2.2) wrapper Dem_DcmGetDTCOfOBDFreezeFrame_Wrapper
 */
Std_ReturnType Dem_DcmGetDTCOfOBDFreezeFrame_Wrapper(uint8 FrameNumber, uint32* DTC)
{
  return DcmGetDTCOfOBDFreezeFrame(FrameNumber, DTC, );
}
/* WA_ESCAN00100457_END: */

